@@ -112,12 +112,26 @@
     O2ContextSetFont(context, _font);
     O2ContextSetFontSize(context, _size);
     /*
-     * A GLYPH POSITION HERE IS ABSOLUTE, and adding the current text position to it was tried and
-     * WITHDRAWN. Quartz documents these as user space, and LibreOffice relies on that: offsetting
-     * them by the text position fixed the CMake descenders and destroyed the LibreOffice Start
-     * Centre, whose labels came back as scattered fragments. The CMake improvement was a
-     * coincidence of whatever value happened to be left in the text position.
+     * A GLYPH POSITION IS AN OFFSET FROM THE TEXT POSITION, AND THIS CALL MUST NOT MOVE IT.
+     *
+     * The two applications that arrive here with their own glyphs disagree about which half they
+     * use, and both are served by the same rule. Qt sets the position and passes zero:
+     *
+     *     CIDER_TEXTPOS set=1.00,1.27 <- QTextureGlyphCache::calculateSubPixelPositionCount
+     *     CIDER_TEXTDRAW ctfont count=1 first=0.00,0.00
+     *
+     * one call per subpixel variant, x stepping 1.00, 1.08, 1.16, 1.25 with y fixed at the lift it
+     * wants under the baseline. LibreOffice goes through Skia, which never sets the position and
+     * passes the offsets itself:
+     *
+     *     CIDER_TEXTDRAW ctfont count=1 first=1.00,2.00 <- SkScalerContext_Mac::Offscreen::getCG
+     *
+     * Adding the base was tried ALONE first and destroyed the LibreOffice Start Centre, because
+     * O2ContextShowGlyphsAtPoint sets the text position as it draws: each call then measured from
+     * where the last one ended and the text walked off the cell. The restore is what makes the rule
+     * hold for both, and it is why this is not simply the earlier change again.
      */
+    O2Point base = O2ContextGetTextPosition(context);
     /* WHETHER THIS ENTRY POINT IS THE ONE IN USE AT ALL. CTFontDrawGlyphs and
      * CGContextShowGlyphsWithAdvances reach the same rasteriser by different routes, and only one
      * of them carries a position per glyph. */
@@ -133,8 +147,10 @@
